Apache Tomcat Maven Plugin

  This is the new home for the Tomcat Maven Plugin (previously hosted at Codehaus).

  Version ${project.version} is the current development version of the Apache Tomcat Maven Plugin.

  More details in {{{./jira-report.html}Generated changelog from issue tracker}}.

  The Apache Tomcat Maven Plugin provides goals to manipulate WAR projects within the {{{http://tomcat.apache.org/}Apache Tomcat}} servlet container.

  * The plugin allows you to:
    ** Run web applications with an embedded Tomcat server
    ** Deploy/undeploy web applications to a running Tomcat server
    ** Create self-contained executable WAR/JAR files with embedded Tomcat

  The plugin supports Tomcat 9, Tomcat 10, and Tomcat 11.

* Plugin Configuration

  Add the plugin to your pom.xml:

+----------
    <plugin>
      <groupId>org.apache.tomcat.maven</groupId>
      <artifactId>tomcat-maven-plugin</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </plugin>
+----------

  Or add the groupId in your settings.xml:

+----------
  <pluginGroups>
    ....
    <pluginGroup>org.apache.tomcat.maven</pluginGroup>
    ....
  </pluginGroups>
+----------

  This allows you to use the shorter goal syntax: tomcat-main:run, tomcat-main:deploy, etc.

